@format 1
@id application.shutdown
@title Application shutdown
@area 1. Application lifecycle
@entry input
@summary Persist window and session state, detach active workspaces, stop relay intake, and flush the log.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related project.save-session
@tag shutdown
@tag session

@alias window = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainWindow.PWindow
@alias scene = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LScene
@alias app = Cadroue.UIShell.PProgram
@alias traceWriter = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LTraceWriter

[input] Window closes <input>
- Receive the main-window close event @ window.PWindowCloseHandle(...)
> persist

[persist] Persist visible state <storage>
- Save the window bounds and timeline height @ window.PWindowCloseHandle(...)
- Capture the current tabs, layouts, exports, relays, and names @ window.PWindowSceneRead(...)
- Save the current session to disk @ scene.LSceneStateSave(...)
> detach

[detach] Detach workspaces <process>
- Unsubscribe the window from relay, tab, options, keyboard, drop, and resize events @ window.PWindowCloseHandle(...)
- Close every tab workspace @ window.PWindowCloseHandle(...)
> exit

[exit] Application exits <output>
- Stop the relay channel @ app.OnExit(...)
- Flush queued trace entries @ traceWriter.LTraceWriterPersist(...)
= Session state is durable and application-owned listeners are detached.
